{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact 15ef792114a105f77b72265b2c689583ef30c1c8 (tree 7291df97c8c4d003156ec735d79c2ca3059bca8c), Main base 1bb0514db2b8911fd2cc589314032f285d6e0cbe, for the joint F2/D2 delivery.\n\n1. P1 — Keep payload availability monotonic across floors (packages/derive/src/floor.ts:44–47,53,95,106; packages/scope/src/sqlite.ts:202–225). After floor 1 deletes a final item's opening entry at position 1, the folded item still exists. A fresh act may legitimately store item-ref 1 on a live item: fields.ts:196 checks the folded item type; this is not a fact read. At floor 2, stateKept adds 1 from that typed value or the retained link act, without consulting the previous floor or requiring history(1). Its queue silently skips the missing payload. SqliteStore.putFloor then inserts 1 into journal_kept even though no entry row exists. archivedPosition now reports 1 as held, while stored(1) remains null. A complete-clone replay's floorOwn exposes entry 1 again because the new kept set names it. Subsequent own fact judgments and reads can therefore disagree between native storage and replay. The source path is established independently and the implementation owner confirmed it in 0e918033; checker has not executed a runtime reproduction.\n\nThe new kept payload positions must be a subset of the previous kept positions plus the previous live tail, even when history contains a complete clone. Preserve valid folded item identities without resurrecting their archived openings. Distinguish identity-only item references from required payload roots: a missing required root must stop the writer/judge/fold rather than be silently skipped. Validate the bounded new kept rows in SQLite before any deletion or other mutation. Add a distinguishing two-floor native/restart and complete-clone replay witness: archive final item 1, admit a fresh link to its folded identity, advance floor 2, keep the link but keep entry 1 absent/archived, refuse its local fact as archived, and reconcile complete checkpoints; include a missing-required-root control. Preserve the submitted candidate and V6 DATA and retain the old-logic failing control separately.\n\nReview scope: primary F2 Source 07b7d066 read first, D2 Source 4e917745 second, then all 99 other submitted Sources and the complete 101-path Main-to-candidate diff. All 101 exact-head Sources were individually inspected; 28 carry inherited staleness, which is preserved and is not a freshness claim. Bounded exact-path artifact inventories at depth 61300 exhausted all six batches (remaining zero). The independent frontier proof finds 96 F2 paths plus five sole D2 paths, with 2,629 unrelated Main leaves preserved byte/blob/mode exactly. The shared core has one F2 Source and a separate D2 provenance assertion for its comment-only citation correction.\n\nNo additional finding emerged from the architecture, authority/read-boundary, or simplification passes over the remaining candidate. In particular, capacity admission checks the post-floor state; no finding is made against the exact-bound capacity path. D2's syntactic inventory has 2,165 scanned files, 1,867 resolved references, 12,668 ambiguous references, five exact listed unresolved findings, zero unlisted broken references and zero listing errors. Independent DATA comparison confirms every resolved section exists uniquely, each known excerpt/hash/single occurrence matches, and the known source and normative files remain identical to Main. This is no claim of semantic compliance with those rules.\n\nValidation: independently copied all 2,783 expressly granted regular V6 DATA leaves only after verifying the exact closed descriptor and row before each copy; originals remained stable and copies physically distinct. All 2,730 captured source leaves match this Git tree in bytes and modes. Prepared/before/launch/after guards reconcile source, 5,498 dependency files and 32 links, tools, package bindings and lock stamp. The natural gate exit